          "note": "1 Aya per relic",
          "alt": "or buy Aya from players at 5-8 p each",
          "done": false
        }
      ],
      "conditions": [
        "Check the live Varzia rotation first: if Mesa is currently unvaulted her relics drop from missions normally and this farm is unnecessary",
        "Take a bounty from Konzu then fail stage 1 on purpose. Every plains camp stays locked at 40-60, so you re-take bounties from the Grineer tents instead of flying back to Cetus",
        "Steel Path adds nothing to Aya rates"
      ],
      "bonuses": [
        "Volt or Nova, not optional: Speed buffs the escort drone, Nova's portal teleports it. Keep the portal exit near ground level and stay close or the drone refuses it",
        "Search and Rescue and Find the Hidden Artifact have the fewest stages that make you stand and wait, 3-5 minutes each",
        "Overfarmed Aya trades at 5-8 p, commonly 6 for 36 p, so a long session is a platinum farm too"
      ],
      "disclosures": [
        {
          "title": "Cambion Drift instead",
          "body": "Lower Aya per bounty but arguably better total return: shorter tilesets, works with almost any frame, and Mother Tokens are uncapped where Cetus standing is not. Tokens buy relic packs, which loop back into relics and Aya, and Endo, Ayatan stars and Kuva accumulate alongside. Bring Nova; Loid still gets stuck on Isolation Vault stages. Orb Vallis gets mentioned but has no rate evidence behind it."
        },
        {
          "title": "traps that eat the tier 5 rate",
          "body": "Flying back to Cetus between bounties. Skipping the fail-stage-1 trick and getting slow low-level bounties. Bringing a frame with no drone support. Cave Exterminate stages and rock-snagged drones. Aya-per-hour numbers from older guides predate the removal of the bounty-rerolling exploit; ~20 an hour is the post-nerf figure."
        }
      ]
    },
